      icon: 'calendar',
      location: 'IBM Innovation Studio, 20 York Road, London, SE1 7ND',
      notes:
        "External.\r\n\r\nThank you for registering for our exclusive in-person event, IBM Network Intelligence – The Future of AI for Smarter Networks.\r\n\r\nEvent Overview\r\n\r\nDate: 13 January 2026\r\nTime: 09:30–12:30\r\nLocation: IBM Innovation Studio, 20 York Road, London, SE1 7ND\r\nHosted by: IBM\r\n\r\nAs networks expand across hybrid and multicloud environments, IT and NetOps teams face mounting pressure to maintain reliability, performance, and agility while operating with fewer resources and lower budgets. This session will explore how IBM is redefining AI for networking, enabling organizations to move from reactive troubleshooting to proactive, autonomous operations.\r\n\r\nWe will dive into how conventional AI falls short, where vendor-specific AI platforms and generic LLMs struggle to interpret network data or understand relationships among devices and services, and this lack of contextual reasoning produce noise rather than clarity. IBM’s approach rethinks AI for networking from the ground up, combining the strengths of data-driven analytics, explainable reasoning and integration with the rest of the business tools to provide context.\r\n\r\nThis event provides a unique opportunity to learn, collaborate, and gain hands-on experience with IBM’s latest advancements.\r\n\r\nAgenda\r\n\r\n09:30 – 10:00 | Reception\r\n10:00 – 10:15 | Welcome & Introduction\r\n10:15 – 10:30 | Challenges & Benefits of AI in Networks\r\n10:30 – 11:15 | Dual-Intelligence AI: IBM Network Intelligence\r\n11:15 – 11:45 | Break & Quantum Computer\r\n11:45 – 12:15 | The Future of Network Observability – SevOne Roadmap\r\n12:15 – 12:30 | Making NetOps More Efficient\r\n12:30 | Lunch & Networking\r\n\r\nIf you need any additional information, please feel free to reach out.\r\n\r\nWe're excited to welcome you to the IBM Innovation Studio and explore the future of AI-powered networking together.\r\n\r\nThanks,\r\nMicheál\r\n",
